## Context

The anti-pattern in 0035 has a class shape: future test scripts can
reintroduce stale-binary execution by defaulting to `tickets/tools/go/erg`.
We need a standing guard that fails when this pattern reappears.

## Actions

1. Add a lightweight regression check to CI or local test harness that
   scans `tests/*.sh` for forbidden default path `tickets/tools/go/erg`.
2. Allow explicit override via `ERG_BIN` but require default path
   `build/erg` for shell integration tests.
3. Document the rule near test conventions.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Regression check exists and runs in `make test` or CI.
- [ ] Check fails if any test script defaults to `tickets/tools/go/erg`.
- [ ] Rule documented for contributors/agents.
